\textbf{Technique: exact affine-slack coupling, finite active-set geometry, Gaussian anti-concentration, and parameter-independent Le Cam transfer.}

Let \(A_\Psi\) have rows \(\alpha_j'\).  Since \(\psi_j(p_0)=0\) for every active cut,
\[
c_n=A_\Psi\sqrt n\{p_n(0)-p_0\}.                                               \tag{12}
\]
The local-family affine-hull condition puts the vector after \(A_\Psi\) in \(\operatorname{lin}(\mathcal P_{\mathrm{ASC}}-p_0)\); hence the definition of \(\mathcal K_0\) yields \(c_n\in\mathcal K_0\).  For every active facet, the exact slack formula gives
\[
\zeta_{n,j}(u)-(\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'u)
=(c_{n,j}-\widehat c_{n,j})+e_{n,j}(u).                                        \tag{13}
\]
Taking the indicated maxima in (13) gives
\[
\max_j\sup_{u\in C}
|\zeta_{n,j}(u)-(\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'u)|
\leq\delta_n(C)+\xi_n\leq\chi_n(C)\leq\overline\chi_n(C).                  \tag{14}
\]

Apply \(\text{lem:finite-completed-arrangement-stability}\) to (14), enlarging its finite active-set constant to include the centered-score displacement \(d_n(C)\), the finitely many rival-union projection systems, and their separation-restoration systems.  This yields simultaneous semantic-label and separated-risk matching at \(\Sigma_0^{-1}\)-displacement at most \(H_C\overline\chi_n(C)\).  This enlargement is finite: on each completed cell and each nearest-face regime, the required correction solves one of finitely many linear systems whose independent row submatrix is known; its norm is bounded by the maximum outward enclosure of the corresponding inverse-basis norms.  Infeasible regimes are discarded by exact rational feasibility.  Equality faces remain in every incident completion.

For every active \(j\), positive definiteness gives \(a_j'\Sigma_0a_j>0\).  Therefore, uniformly in the mean and in the offset, the one-dimensional normal density gives
\[
\Pr_h\{|\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'W_0|\leq s\}
\leq\min\left\{1,
\frac{2s}{\sqrt{2\pi}\{a_j'\Sigma_0a_j\}^{1/2}}\right\}.                  \tag{15}
\]
Take the collar width to be \(\tau_n=\overline\chi_n(C)\).  By (14), a sign can differ only if the reference slack lies in the band of width
\(\tau_n+\chi_n(C)\leq2\overline\chi_n(C)\); moreover the exceptional indicator \(\mathbf1\{\chi_n(C)>\tau_n\}\) is zero.  Summing (15) over the finite active list therefore gives
\[
\mathfrak b_0\{\tau_n+\chi_n(C)\}
\leq\mathfrak b_0\{2\overline\chi_n(C)\}
\leq2A_0\overline\chi_n(C).                                                    \tag{16}
\]

By \(\text{prop:carter-fixed-m-positive-cell}\), Carter's parameter-independent kernel contributes
\[
C_{2/\kappa}\frac{|\mathcal J|\log|\mathcal J|}{\sqrt n}.                   \tag{17}
\]
The score-normal mean and covariance calculation in the proof of \(\text{thm:fixed-stratum-transfer}\), with the moving base \(p_n(0)\), contributes \(\operatorname{Err}_{\Sigma,n}(C)\).  Equal-covariance Gaussian translation for the matching displacement contributes the \(H_C\overline\chi_n(C)\) term.  Applying \(\text{lem:bounded-semantic-transfer-by-tv}\) to coverage indicators and to \(\ell_0\in[0,1]\), and adding (16)--(17), proves (11).  The Carter term tends to zero, \(\operatorname{Err}_{\Sigma,n}(C)\to0\) by \(\text{lem:compact-moving-remainder-covariance}\), and the last term tends to zero whenever \(\overline\chi_n(C)\to0\).  No effective modulus was used.
